  "S4_energy": "A@K5: E_driver 534.0 fJ/bank/cycle = 2.22x the 240.292 fJ ledger; overhead +122.2%, N-invariant. >100% -> CLOSES per the pre-registered line. B/C: close on S1/S3 before S4.",
  "headline": "THE FLAT TOP IS BUILDABLE AND THE 12x SURVIVES -- the harmonic-sum driver (DC + harmonics 1,2,4,5; the 3k harmonics are geometrically ABSENT) reproduces the committed 129 ps standing eye on a fully driven mesh at 33.5 mV droop -- but it costs 534 fJ/bank/cycle against the 240.3 fJ ledger (+122%, B-invariant, unamortisable) on the MEASURED eta_amp=25.46% sustainer record. No candidate fits the <=25% band; stepped/clamped (B) and switched-LC (C) fail the spec outright on this load (the hold-third corruption drain admits no ZCS and punishes every clamp). Per the pre-registration this CLOSES the mesh route's flat-top rider at current sustainer efficiency: the 12.0x stands only if 2.2x per-bank energy is an acceptable price for 12x wavefront throughput. The eta needed for the 25% band is 62% -- far beyond every measured point on the committed ladder (max 33% at Q=50).",
  "pre_stated_pick_outcome": "FALSIFIED. The pre-registered pick (C admitted at N>=4-8) was wrong on both counts: C cannot even meet droop on the real load, and the candidate predicted to close on S4 (A) is the only one that meets the electrical spec. Logged as the round's headline correction.",
